quest - Inbound - REST API Explorer#{37}":[1087,1088],"#REST category#Related":[1089,1092],"#REST category#Related#{1}":[1091,1092]},"outlinks":[{"title":"REST APIs","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/c_RESTAPI.md","line":38},{"title":"REST APIs","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/c_RESTAPI.md","line":113},{"title":"Application scope","target":"c_ApplicationScope","line":145},{"title":"Automated Test Framework roles","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/application-development/automated-test-framework-atf/atf-roles.md","line":187},{"title":"Create a basic auth profile using the Automated Test Framework","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/application-development/automated-test-framework-atf/atf-create-basic-auth-profile.md","line":195},{"title":"Set up Certificate-based authentication","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-security/set-up-mutual-auth.md","line":203},{"title":"Importing JSON files","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/integrate-applications/json-data-source-examples.md","line":952},{"title":"Application scope","target":"c_ApplicationScope","line":1091}],"metadata":{"title":"REST category","description":"Verify the functionality of REST calls.This test step begins with the REST API Explorer. Use the REST API Explorer to create and specify the HTTP method, path, query parameters, request headers, and body of a REST request, and then send the REST request to the current instance.Create a test step to send a REST request to the current instance. Specify the HTTP method, path, query parameters, request headers, and body of a REST request.Assert that the HTTP response status code has the specified relationship to the specified value. You specify a numeric value of the status code and the relationship.Assert that the HTTP response status code name has the specified relationship to the specified value. You specify a value of the status code name, and the relationship.Assert that the HTTP response time has the specified relationship to the specified value. You specify a value of the response time and the relationship.Assert the HTTP response header exists, or the header has the specified relationship to the specified value.Assert that the response payload is in valid JSON format.Assert that the response payload is well-formed XML.Assert the XML response payload element exists, or has the specified relationship to the specified value.Assert the JSON response payload element exists, or has the specified relationship to the specified value.Assert the HTTP response payload has the specified relationship to the specified value. You specify the value and the relationship.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/application-development/automated-test-framework-atf/test-steps-rest-category.html","release":"australia","product":"Automated Test Framework \\(ATF\\)","classification":"automated-test-framework-atf","topic_type":"reference","last_updated":"2026-03-12","reading_time_minutes":15,"breadcrumb":["Automated Test Framework \\(ATF\\) test step categories","Automated Test Framework \\(ATF\\)","Testing and debugging applications","Building applications"],"tags":["#application-development","#atf","#testing","#automated-tests","#test-suites","#type-reference"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[[844,950],[1072,1074],[1078,1080]],"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/application-development/automated-test-framework-atf/test-steps-rest-category.md"},
